module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.TrivSqZeroExt.Ideal
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Flat.Basic
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Module.OppositeOfCommSemiring
public import StacksFrontier.Deformation.Examples.RingsSmooth
public import StacksFrontier.Deformation.SquareZero.AlgebraExtensions
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Flat.SquareZeroConormal

/-!
# The kernel of the reduction of a ring deformation

A flat deformation of a `k`-algebra `P` over the dual numbers reduces to `P` with a
square-zero kernel. This file equips that kernel with its `P`-module structure, which is
the first half of the identification of the tangent space of the deformation category of
`P` with the isomorphism classes of square-zero extensions of `P` by `P`.

The second half is the identification of the kernel itself. Let `V` be a `k`-vector space,
let `k ⊕ V` be the square-zero extension of Stacks 06IB, and let `Q` be a flat `k ⊕ V`-algebra
whose reduction along the augmentation is `P` and whose kernel is generated by the augmentation
ideal. Then the canonical `k`-linear map `P ⊗[k] V → Q`, carrying `p ⊗ v` to `v · q` for any
lift `q` of `p`, is a bijection onto the kernel of `Q → P`: so a first-order flat deformation
of `P` over `k ⊕ V` is a square-zero extension of `P` by `P ⊗[k] V`, which is the shape in
which Stacks 0GPT classifies it by `Ext¹_P(NL_{P/k}, P ⊗[k] V)`. This is the commutative-algebra
content of the tangent-space clause of Stacks 0DY3, and the step that both
`StacksFrontier/Deformation/Examples/Geometric/RingsTangentSpaceFinite.lean` (Stacks 0DY4(2)) and
`StacksFrontier/Deformation/Examples/Geometric/RingsHypersurfaceTangentSpace.lean` (Stacks 0DY5(2))
record as missing.

## Main definitions

* `Deformation.Examples.kernelModule` is the `P`-module structure on the kernel of a
  square-zero reduction `Q → P`, obtained by descending the `Q`-action.
* `Deformation.Examples.IsFirstOrderReduction` says that the reduction `Q → P` is compatible
  with the augmentation `k ⊕ V → k`.
* `Deformation.Examples.firstOrderConormalHom` is the canonical map `P ⊗[k] V → Q`.

## Main results

* `Deformation.Examples.firstOrderConormalHom_tmul`: the canonical map is computed by any lift,
  so it does not depend on the chosen section.
* `Deformation.Examples.firstOrderConormalHom_smul`: it is semilinear for the reduction, scaling
  by `p` upstairs being multiplication by any lift of `p`.
* `Deformation.Examples.reduction_firstOrderConormalHom` and
  `Deformation.Examples.exists_firstOrderConormalHom_eq`: its image is exactly the kernel of the
  reduction.
* `Deformation.Examples.injective_firstOrderConormalHom`: it is injective, which is where
  flatness of `Q` over `k ⊕ V` is used.

## Implementation notes

The `Q`-action on the kernel `I` of `Q → P` descends to `Q ⧸ I`, and hence to `P`, because
`I * I ⊆ I ^ 2 = 0`. The descent is carried out by `Quotient.liftOn`, so the module
structure is produced without any choice: no set-theoretic section of `Q → P` is taken,
and no element is obtained from an existence statement. Concretely the scalar action is
defined on `Q ⧸ I` by `Quotient.liftOn`, promoted to a module structure by
`Function.Surjective.moduleLeft` along `Ideal.Quotient.mk I` — whose side condition holds
by `rfl` precisely because the action was defined by that lift — and transported to `P`
along the ring isomorphism `P ≃+* Q ⧸ I` of `RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective`.

The route through `Ideal.Cotangent` does not work, and the reason is worth recording.
`Ideal.Cotangent I` does carry a `Module (Q ⧸ I)` structure, and for a square-zero ideal
`Ideal.cotangentEquivOfSqZero` identifies it with `I`; but that identification is
`Q`-linear, not `(Q ⧸ I)`-linear, so it does not transport the quotient-ring module
structure, which is the only thing wanted from it.

The canonical map `P ⊗[k] V → Q` is built from a `k`-linear section of the reduction, which
exists because the reduction is a surjection of `k`-vector spaces; the resulting map does not
depend on the section, because two lifts of the same element differ by an element of the kernel
and the augmentation ideal annihilates the kernel. Its injectivity is not proved directly: the
canonical map of Stacks 063Y, `I ⊗[k ⊕ V] Q → Q` for `I` the augmentation ideal, factors as the
canonical map here composed with a surjection `I ⊗[k ⊕ V] Q → P ⊗[k] V`, and flatness of `Q`
makes that canonical map injective, which forces injectivity here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0DY3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0DY3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 063Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063Y)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GPT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GPT)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

universe w

namespace Deformation.Examples

section
variable {k P Q : Type w} [Field k] [CommRing P] [Algebra k P] [CommRing Q] [Algebra k Q]


/-- Scalar multiplication of the reduced ring on the kernel of a square-zero reduction. -/
@[instance_reducible]
public def kernelSMul (π : Q →ₐ[k] P)
    (hI2 : RingHom.ker π.toRingHom ^ 2 = ⊥) :
    SMul (Q ⧸ RingHom.ker π.toRingHom) ↥(RingHom.ker π.toRingHom) where
  smul c x := Quotient.liftOn c (fun q => q • x) (fun a b hab => by
    have h : a - b ∈ RingHom.ker π.toRingHom := (Submodule.quotientRel_def _).1 hab
    have hm : (a - b) * (x : Q) = 0 := by
      have hmem : (a - b) * (x : Q) ∈ RingHom.ker π.toRingHom ^ 2 := by
        rw [pow_two]
        exact Ideal.mul_mem_mul h x.2
      rw [hI2] at hmem
      simpa using hmem
    refine Subtype.val_injective ?_
    change a • (x : Q) = b • (x : Q)
    rw [smul_eq_mul, smul_eq_mul]
    exact sub_eq_zero.1 (by rw [← sub_mul]; exact hm))

/-- The kernel of a square-zero reduction is a module over the quotient. -/
@[instance_reducible]
public def kernelModuleQuotient (π : Q →ₐ[k] P)
    (hI2 : RingHom.ker π.toRingHom ^ 2 = ⊥) :
    Module (Q ⧸ RingHom.ker π.toRingHom) ↥(RingHom.ker π.toRingHom) :=
  letI := kernelSMul π hI2
  Function.Surjective.moduleLeft (Ideal.Quotient.mk (RingHom.ker π.toRingHom))
    Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective (fun _ _ => rfl)


/-- The reduced ring of a surjection is the quotient by its kernel. -/
public noncomputable def quotKerRingEquiv (π : Q →ₐ[k] P) (hsurj : Function.Surjective π) :
    P ≃+* (Q ⧸ RingHom.ker π.toRingHom) :=
  (RingHom.quotientKerEquivOfSurjective (f := π.toRingHom) hsurj).symm

/-- The kernel of a square-zero reduction `Q → P` is a `P`-module: the `Q`-action descends
because the kernel annihilates itself. -/
@[instance_reducible]
public noncomputable def kernelModule (π : Q →ₐ[k] P) (hsurj : Function.Surjective π)
    (hI2 : RingHom.ker π.toRingHom ^ 2 = ⊥) :
    Module P ↥(RingHom.ker π.toRingHom) :=
  letI := kernelModuleQuotient π hI2
  Module.compHom _ (quotKerRingEquiv π hsurj).toRingHom

end

open TensorProduct TrivSqZeroExt

section FirstOrder

variable {k : Type w} [Field k] {V : Type w} [AddCommGroup V] [Module k V]

/-- The right action of `k` on `V`, through `MulOpposite.unop`. -/
local instance : Module kᵐᵒᵖ V :=
  Module.oppositeOfCommSemiring k V

/-- The left and right actions of `k` on `V` agree. -/
local instance : IsCentralScalar k V := Module.isCentralScalar_oppositeOfCommSemiring k V

variable {P Q : Type w} [CommRing P] [Algebra k P] [CommRing Q]
  [Algebra (TrivSqZeroExt k V) Q] [Algebra k Q]
  [IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) Q]

omit [Algebra k Q] [IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) Q] in
/-- The augmentation ideal of `k ⊕ V` annihilates the submodule of `Q` it generates. -/
public theorem kerIdeal_smul_eq_zero {i : TrivSqZeroExt k V} (hi : i ∈ kerIdeal k V) {x : Q}
    (hx : x ∈ kerIdeal k V • (⊤ : Submodule (TrivSqZeroExt k V) Q)) : i • x = 0 := by
  have h : i • x ∈ kerIdeal k V • (kerIdeal k V • (⊤ : Submodule (TrivSqZeroExt k V) Q)) :=
    Submodule.smul_mem_smul hi hx
  rw [← Submodule.smul_assoc, Ideal.smul_eq_mul, ← pow_two, kerIdeal_sq, Submodule.bot_smul,
    Submodule.mem_bot] at h
  exact h

variable (π : Q →ₐ[k] P)

/-- A `k`-linear section of the reduction of a first-order deformation. -/
public def reductionSection (hπ : Function.Surjective π) : P →ₗ[k] Q :=
  (LinearMap.exists_rightInverse_of_surjective π.toLinearMap
    (LinearMap.range_eq_top.mpr hπ)).choose

/-- The chosen section is a section: the reduction sends `reductionSection π hπ p` to `p`. -/
public theorem apply_reductionSection (hπ : Function.Surjective π) (p : P) :
    π (reductionSection π hπ p) = p :=
  DFunLike.congr_fun (LinearMap.exists_rightInverse_of_surjective π.toLinearMap
    (LinearMap.range_eq_top.mpr hπ)).choose_spec p

/-- The action of `c : k` on `Q` is the action of its image in `k ⊕ V`. -/
public theorem algebraMap_smul_eq (c : k) (x : Q) :
    c • x = (algebraMap k (TrivSqZeroExt k V)) c • x :=
  (IsScalarTower.algebraMap_smul (TrivSqZeroExt k V) c x).symm

/-- The action of `inr v` on `Q` commutes with the action of scalars of `k`. -/
public theorem inr_smul_comm (c : k) (v : V) (x : Q) :
    (inr v : TrivSqZeroExt k V) • (c • x) = c • ((inr v : TrivSqZeroExt k V) • x) := by
  rw [algebraMap_smul_eq (V := V) c x,
    algebraMap_smul_eq (V := V) c ((inr v : TrivSqZeroExt k V) • x), smul_smul, smul_smul,
    mul_comm]

/-- The action of `inr (c • v)` on `Q` is `c` times the action of `inr v`. -/
public theorem inr_smul_scalar (c : k) (v : V) (x : Q) :
    (inr (c • v) : TrivSqZeroExt k V) • x = c • ((inr v : TrivSqZeroExt k V) • x) := by
  have h : (inr (c • v) : TrivSqZeroExt k V)
      = (algebraMap k (TrivSqZeroExt k V)) c * inr v := by
    simp only [algebraMap_eq_inl]
    exact (inl_mul_inr c v).symm
  rw [h, ← smul_smul, ← algebraMap_smul_eq (V := V)]

/-- The bilinear map `(p, v) ↦ v · q` for `q` the chosen lift of `p`. -/
public def firstOrderConormalBilin (hπ : Function.Surjective π) : P →ₗ[k] V →ₗ[k] Q :=
  LinearMap.mk₂ k (fun p v ↦ (inr v : TrivSqZeroExt k V) • reductionSection π hπ p)
    (fun _ _ _ ↦ by rw [map_add, smul_add])
    (fun _ _ _ ↦ by rw [map_smul, inr_smul_comm])
    (fun _ _ _ ↦ by rw [inr_add, add_smul])
    (fun c _ v ↦ inr_smul_scalar c v _)

/-- **The conormal module of a first-order deformation.** Let `Q` be a flat `k ⊕ V`-algebra
whose reduction along the augmentation is `P`. This is the canonical `k`-linear map
`P ⊗[k] V → Q` carrying `p ⊗ v` to `v · q` for `q` a lift of `p`; the value does not depend on
the lift, by `Deformation.Examples.firstOrderConormalHom_tmul`. Its image is the kernel of the
reduction and it is injective, so it identifies `P ⊗[k] V` with that kernel.

The chosen lift is produced by a `k`-linear section of the reduction, which exists because `P`
and `Q` are `k`-vector spaces; nothing depends on which section is taken. -/
public def firstOrderConormalHom (hπ : Function.Surjective π) : P ⊗[k] V →ₗ[k] Q :=
  TensorProduct.lift (firstOrderConormalBilin π hπ)

/-- The canonical map is computed by any lift, not only the chosen one. -/
public theorem firstOrderConormalHom_tmul (hπ : Function.Surjective π)
    (hker : ∀ x : Q, π x = 0 → x ∈ kerIdeal k V • (⊤ : Submodule (TrivSqZeroExt k V) Q))
    (p : P) (v : V) (q : Q) (hq : π q = p) :
    firstOrderConormalHom π hπ (p ⊗ₜ[k] v) = (inr v : TrivSqZeroExt k V) • q := by
  have hmem : q - reductionSection π hπ p ∈
      kerIdeal k V • (⊤ : Submodule (TrivSqZeroExt k V) Q) := by
    refine hker _ ?_
    rw [map_sub, hq, apply_reductionSection, sub_self]
  have h0 : (inr v : TrivSqZeroExt k V) • (q - reductionSection π hπ p) = 0 :=
    kerIdeal_smul_eq_zero ((mem_kerIdeal_iff_inr k V _).2 rfl) hmem
  rw [smul_sub, sub_eq_zero] at h0
  change (inr v : TrivSqZeroExt k V) • reductionSection π hπ p = _
  exact h0.symm

/-- The canonical map is semilinear for the reduction: scaling by `p'` upstairs is
multiplication by any lift of `p'`. -/
public theorem firstOrderConormalHom_smul (hπ : Function.Surjective π)
    (hker : ∀ x : Q, π x = 0 → x ∈ kerIdeal k V • (⊤ : Submodule (TrivSqZeroExt k V) Q))
    (p' : P) (q' : Q) (hq' : π q' = p') (x : P ⊗[k] V) :
    firstOrderConormalHom (V := V) π hπ (p' • x)
      = q' * firstOrderConormalHom (V := V) π hπ x := by
  induction x with
  | zero => simp
  | tmul p v =>
    rw [TensorProduct.smul_tmul', smul_eq_mul,
      firstOrderConormalHom_tmul π hπ hker _ _ (q' * (reductionSection π hπ p))
        (by rw [map_mul, hq', apply_reductionSection]),
      firstOrderConormalHom_tmul π hπ hker _ _ (reductionSection π hπ p)
        (apply_reductionSection π hπ p),
      Algebra.smul_def, Algebra.smul_def]
    ring
  | add x y hx hy => rw [smul_add, map_add, map_add, hx, hy, mul_add]

/-- The reduction `Q → P` is compatible with the augmentation `k ⊕ V → k`: the structural map
of `Q` followed by the reduction is the first projection followed by the structural map of
`P`. -/
public abbrev IsFirstOrderReduction (V : Type w) [AddCommGroup V] [Module k V] [Module kᵐᵒᵖ V]
    [IsCentralScalar k V] {P Q : Type w} [CommRing P] [Algebra k P] [CommRing Q]
    [Algebra k Q] [Algebra (TrivSqZeroExt k V) Q] (π : Q →ₐ[k] P) : Prop :=
  ∀ a : TrivSqZeroExt k V,
    π (algebraMap (TrivSqZeroExt k V) Q a) = algebraMap k P a.fst

omit [IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) Q] in
private theorem map_smul_apply (hπa : IsFirstOrderReduction V π) (a : TrivSqZeroExt k V) (q : Q) :
    π (a • q) = algebraMap k P a.fst * π q := by
  rw [Algebra.smul_def, map_mul, hπa]

/-- The canonical map lands in the kernel of the reduction, since the augmentation ideal does
so. -/
public theorem reduction_firstOrderConormalHom (hπ : Function.Surjective π)
    (hπa : IsFirstOrderReduction V π) (x : P ⊗[k] V) :
    π (firstOrderConormalHom π hπ x) = 0 := by
  induction x with
  | zero => simp
  | tmul p v =>
    change π ((inr v : TrivSqZeroExt k V) • reductionSection π hπ p) = 0
    rw [map_smul_apply π hπa, fst_inr, map_zero, zero_mul]
  | add x y hx hy => rw [map_add, map_add, hx, hy, add_zero]

/-- `k ⊕ V` acts on `P ⊗[k] V` through its first coordinate. -/
local instance : Module (TrivSqZeroExt k V) (P ⊗[k] V) :=
  Module.compHom _ (fstHom k k V).toRingHom

/-- The actions of `k` and of `k ⊕ V` on `P ⊗[k] V` form a scalar tower. -/
local instance : IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) (P ⊗[k] V) :=
  IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_smul fun _ _ ↦ rfl

private theorem coe_kerIdeal_fst (i : ↥(kerIdeal k V)) :
    (i : TrivSqZeroExt k V).fst = 0 := by
  rw [(mem_kerIdeal_iff_inr k V (i : TrivSqZeroExt k V)).1 i.2, fst_inr]

private theorem coe_kerIdeal_smul_snd (a : TrivSqZeroExt k V) (i : ↥(kerIdeal k V)) :
    ((a • i : ↥(kerIdeal k V)) : TrivSqZeroExt k V).snd
      = a.fst • (i : TrivSqZeroExt k V).snd := by
  change (a * (i : TrivSqZeroExt k V)).snd = _
  rw [snd_mul, coe_kerIdeal_fst]
  simp

/-- The bilinear map `(i, q) ↦ π q ⊗ i` on the augmentation ideal, whose induced map on the
tensor product is the surjection `I ⊗[k ⊕ V] Q → P ⊗[k] V`. -/
private def conormalCompareBilin (hπa : IsFirstOrderReduction V π) :
    ↥(kerIdeal k V) →ₗ[TrivSqZeroExt k V] Q →ₗ[TrivSqZeroExt k V] P ⊗[k] V :=
  LinearMap.mk₂ (TrivSqZeroExt k V)
    (fun i q ↦ π q ⊗ₜ[k] (i : TrivSqZeroExt k V).snd)
    (fun i₁ i₂ q ↦ by
      change π q ⊗ₜ[k] ((i₁ + i₂ : ↥(kerIdeal k V)) : TrivSqZeroExt k V).snd = _
      change _ = π q ⊗ₜ[k] (i₁ : TrivSqZeroExt k V).snd + π q ⊗ₜ[k] (i₂ : TrivSqZeroExt k V).snd
      rw [← TensorProduct.tmul_add]
      rfl)
    (fun a i q ↦ by
      change π q ⊗ₜ[k] ((a • i : ↥(kerIdeal k V)) : TrivSqZeroExt k V).snd = _
      change _ = a.fst • (π q ⊗ₜ[k] (i : TrivSqZeroExt k V).snd)
      rw [coe_kerIdeal_smul_snd, TensorProduct.tmul_smul])
    (fun _ _ _ ↦ by rw [map_add, TensorProduct.add_tmul])
    (fun a i q ↦ by
      change π (a • q) ⊗ₜ[k] (i : TrivSqZeroExt k V).snd = _
      change _ = a.fst • (π q ⊗ₜ[k] (i : TrivSqZeroExt k V).snd)
      rw [map_smul_apply π hπa, ← Algebra.smul_def, TensorProduct.smul_tmul'])

/-- The surjection `I ⊗[k ⊕ V] Q → P ⊗[k] V` through which the canonical map of Stacks 063Y
factors. -/
private def conormalCompare (hπa : IsFirstOrderReduction V π) :
    ↥(kerIdeal k V) ⊗[TrivSqZeroExt k V] Q →ₗ[TrivSqZeroExt k V] P ⊗[k] V :=
  TensorProduct.lift (conormalCompareBilin π hπa)

omit [IsScalarTower k (TrivSqZeroExt k V) Q] in
private theorem conormalCompare_surjective (hπa : IsFirstOrderReduction V π)
    (hπ : Function.Surjective π) :
    Function.Surjective (conormalCompare π hπa) := by
  intro x
  induction x with
  | zero => exact ⟨0, map_zero _⟩
  | tmul p v =>
    obtain ⟨q, hq⟩ := hπ p
    refine ⟨(⟨inr v, (mem_kerIdeal_iff_inr k V _).2 rfl⟩ : ↥(kerIdeal k V)) ⊗ₜ q, ?_⟩
    change π q ⊗ₜ[k] (inr v : TrivSqZeroExt k V).snd = _
    rw [snd_inr, hq]
  | add x y hx hy =>
    obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := hx
    obtain ⟨w, hw⟩ := hy
    exact ⟨z + w, by rw [map_add, hz, hw]⟩

private theorem firstOrderConormalHom_conormalCompare (hπa : IsFirstOrderReduction V π)
    (hπ : Function.Surjective π)
    (hker : ∀ x : Q, π x = 0 → x ∈ kerIdeal k V • (⊤ : Submodule (TrivSqZeroExt k V) Q))
    (z : ↥(kerIdeal k V) ⊗[TrivSqZeroExt k V] Q) :
    firstOrderConormalHom π hπ (conormalCompare π hπa z)
      = (kerIdeal k V).tensorSMulHom Q z := by
  induction z with
  | zero => simp
  | tmul i q =>
    change firstOrderConormalHom π hπ (π q ⊗ₜ[k] (i : TrivSqZeroExt k V).snd)
      = (i : TrivSqZeroExt k V) • q
    rw [firstOrderConormalHom_tmul π hπ hker _ _ q rfl,
      ← (mem_kerIdeal_iff_inr k V (i : TrivSqZeroExt k V)).1 i.2]
  | add z w hz hw => simp only [map_add, hz, hw]

/-- **The kernel of a first-order flat deformation is `P ⊗[k] V`: injectivity.** This is where
flatness of `Q` over `k ⊕ V` enters, through the commutative-algebra heart of Stacks 063Y:
flatness makes `I ⊗[k ⊕ V] Q → Q` injective for the augmentation ideal `I`, and the canonical
map factors that one through the surjection `I ⊗[k ⊕ V] Q → P ⊗[k] V`. -/
public theorem injective_firstOrderConormalHom [Module.Flat (TrivSqZeroExt k V) Q]
    (hπa : IsFirstOrderReduction V π) (hπ : Function.Surjective π)
    (hker : ∀ x : Q, π x = 0 → x ∈ kerIdeal k V • (⊤ : Submodule (TrivSqZeroExt k V) Q)) :
    Function.Injective (firstOrderConormalHom (V := V) π hπ) := by
  have hτ : Function.Injective ((kerIdeal k V).tensorSMulHom Q) :=
    ((kerIdeal k V).injective_tensorSMulHom_iff Q).2
      (Module.Flat.rTensor_preserves_injective_linearMap (M := Q)
        (kerIdeal k V).subtype Subtype.val_injective)
  refine (injective_iff_map_eq_zero _).2 fun x hx ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨z, rfl⟩ := conormalCompare_surjective π hπa hπ x
  rw [firstOrderConormalHom_conormalCompare π hπa hπ hker] at hx
  have hz0 : (kerIdeal k V).tensorSMulHom Q z = (kerIdeal k V).tensorSMulHom Q 0 := by
    rw [hx, map_zero]
  rw [hτ hz0, map_zero]

/-- **The kernel of a first-order flat deformation is `P ⊗[k] V`: surjectivity.** Every element
of the kernel of the reduction is the image of an element of `P ⊗[k] V`, because the kernel is
`I · Q` and so is the image of `I ⊗[k ⊕ V] Q → Q`. -/
public theorem exists_firstOrderConormalHom_eq (hπa : IsFirstOrderReduction V π)
    (hπ : Function.Surjective π)
    (hker : ∀ x : Q, π x = 0 → x ∈ kerIdeal k V • (⊤ : Submodule (TrivSqZeroExt k V) Q))
    {y : Q} (hy : π y = 0) : ∃ x, firstOrderConormalHom (V := V) π hπ x = y := by
  have hmem : y ∈ LinearMap.range ((kerIdeal k V).tensorSMulHom Q) := by
    rw [(kerIdeal k V).range_tensorSMulHom Q]
    exact hker y hy
  obtain ⟨z, hz⟩ := hmem
  exact ⟨conormalCompare π hπa z,
    (firstOrderConormalHom_conormalCompare π hπa hπ hker z).trans hz⟩

end FirstOrder

end Deformation.Examples
